            "email": "noreply@github.com",
            "date": "2026-08-31T17:19:19Z"
          },
          "message": "Only spell out a standalone 1 in the English number normalizer (#2836)\n\n`\\b` also matches next to \".\", \"$\", \"%\" and \"-\", so the readability rule\nthat rewrites the digit 1 as \"one\" fired inside numbers as well:\n\"three point one\" gave \"3 one\", \"one point five\" gave \"one.5\",\n\"one dollar\" gave \" one\" and \"one percent\" gave \"one \".\n\nRequire whitespace on both sides so only a lone 1 is rewritten. The\nexisting tests already pin the shape for the neighboring values\n(\"3 point 2\" -> \"3.2\", \"3 cents\" -> \"\u00a23\", \"ninety percent\" -> \"90%\",\n\"minus 500\" -> \"-500\"); the value one now matches them.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TLWefdPAbf8QT4fS8Pkk68\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "f7b3cb8e12a2e84dccacc4c858c33d5a9c114688",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/openai/whisper/git/trees/f7b3cb8e12a2e84dccacc4c858c33d5a9c114688"
          },
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/openai/whisper/git/commits/86098128c0b4f24f0e2aa2994de830614b474227",
          "comment_count": 0,
          "verification": {
            "verified": true,
            "reason": "valid",
            "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlbeXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaesQACufuQMQFmNKgMh7Ziil7iY8\nlykQMAHKUwEjNj7VUTPfmZ+VTMtM98Fn9saGuADdgP4xGGlf1pXwfDRrRgBPNZ18\nelccjhCHfKNnCYX4JRK9svsn1XrZ+XAazLDImJ+vdIfVyLxsIdZbn46K3jo2VAtZ\n7EwZali1Zf5JHgof4/OzBhX9MrcLLRVBUgIoBLGiYi4aNDUMgJBAvsqpW+4sYKxj\nYPqg2t3v2GI1JglT/IBOZdkZdtHomG3KIGAoRyd6Fzvnw6e6+n+Nl6g3rrASkaZh\nbsXrPED2iHCUz9uw4KhwmEJb3g15IT/yUnn7SAvu2/O2Vnlt8Mc8fRFKNxh9EmNb\nU2x1usDyKcWMkUU5RcbAKtstkjtpQJwPpAmFyvIHhyiKb3tvwjsmvK/MFgaWVo2T\npjquDl5CVtuIZceQBKvK0Vny4a88K45Q3AS7gIv/nrhewu5LIHwhof4NBCSzCl2P\npaudT/8xTM/hNkZ8Kb1wm7zOUhpI69+1cqOVB8efmAg4WJWHdAYHXPY4nn91acOa\nNk0eHn6ma4+TDgtHJ0qSMTEi/x74m5U0gwTbFNlard30B1PVLie/wgHQ7PkGp7iB\nIYcbSAEtSsdARvXHPxrifHXMccXxApKDoNYOZTi6HzN6bq8nEBduxR0gNu+fYfL+\n27FUxVKIL6HJS3Bvt9/A\n=SBQV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
            "payload": "tree f7b3cb8e12a2e84dccacc4c858c33d5a9c114688\nparent 5f86d1d86363843179951550570367b37c5d6f78\nauthor Kayvan Zahiri <123409429+Kayvan-Zahiri@users.noreply.github.com> 1788196759 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788196759 -0700\n\nOnly spell out a standalone 1 in the English number normalizer (#2836)\n\n`\\b` also matches next to \".\", \"$\", \"%\" and \"-\", so the readability rule\nthat rewrites the digit 1 as \"one\" fired inside numbers as well:\n\"three point one\" gave \"3 one\", \"one point five\" gave \"one.5\",\n\"one dollar\" gave \" one\" and \"one percent\" gave \"one \".\n\nRequire whitespace on both sides so only a lone 1 is rewritten. The\nexisting tests already pin the shape for the neighboring values\n(\"3 point 2\" -> \"3.2\", \"3 cents\" -> \"\u00a23\", \"ninety percent\" -> \"90%\",\n\"minus 500\" -> \"-500\"); the value one now matches them.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TLWefdPAbf8QT4fS8Pkk68\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
